# #
#   This file contains configuration elements for the CF_ENABLE CloudFlare feature
#   
#   Entries:
#   
#   DOMAIN:     These list the per domain CloudFlare credientials for each matching domain
#               for all relevant triggers (i.e. LF_MODSEC)
#   
#               The special case "any" can be used as the domain name for all relevant
#               triggers regardless of domain
#   
#   USER:       This must be a unique name for the entry, but does not have to be a local
#               linux account name
#   
#   CFACCOUNT:  This is the CloudFlare login user (email address), or the word
#               "token" to authenticate with a CloudFlare API token instead of
#               the Global API Key
#   
#   CFAPIKEY:   This is the CloudFlare Global API Key, or the API token when
#               CFACCOUNT is "token". The token needs the user-level
#               "Firewall Access Rules: Edit" permission (or the zone-level
#               equivalent for the zones you protect)
#   
#   DISABLE:    Normally, comment out a line to disable it. On servers with CF_CPANEL enabled
#               a cPanel user can be disabled here
#   
#   ANY:        On servers with CF_CPANEL enabled a cPanel user can be configured to use the
#               special "any" case (see above)
# #

# #
#   CloudFlare client credientials for any domain triggered:
# #

#   DOMAIN:any:USER:myuser:CFACCOUNT:sales@hostsdomain.com:CFAPIKEY:12345abcdef6789

# #
#   CloudFlare client credientials for domain.com involved in trigger:
# #

#   DOMAIN:domain.com:USER:myuser:CFACCOUNT:sales@domain.com:CFAPIKEY:12345abcdef6789

# #
#   CloudFlare client credientials for domain2.com involved in trigger:
# #

#   DOMAIN:domain2.com:USER:myuser:CFACCOUNT:myuser@hotmail.com:CFAPIKEY:12345abcdef6789

# #
#   CloudFlare API token (Bearer auth) for any domain triggered, instead of
#   the Global API Key:
# #

#   DOMAIN:any:USER:myuser:CFACCOUNT:token:CFAPIKEY:your_cloudflare_api_token

# #
#   Disable CloudFlare cPanel user mycpanel from this feature:
# #

#   DISABLE:mycpanel

# #
#   Enable a cPanel user mycpanel to use the "any" feature:
# #

#   ANY:mycpanel
